Open the SETTINGS sub-screen: clicking the SETTINGS menu item (state 0x6) now enters its full screen
loop and renders the SETTINGS.MRL background, mirroring the ABOUT dialog flow (patch 129).

The menu-item activate (ea5a, patch 129) writes the item's target screen state to DGROUP:0xf78e; the
e714 tail jumptable (image 0xe77a, state = byte offset) dispatches it.  SETTINGS = state 0x6 -> _tgt
0xe94f = `e39f(); call 6a4a; jmp e714` (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin) -- a full SCREEN
(not a modal dialog like ABOUT's 7088).  6a4a builds a display list from template seg 0x2c41 (size
0x148) and runs the standard paint/event loop until the exit flag DAT_2000_4a92 (DGROUP:0x8a92).

Sub-fixes (all asm-verified):
